  <title>Unary minus after a relation (issue 535)</title>
  <para xml:id="p1">
    <p>Both operands present <Math mode="inline" tex="a=-b" text="a = - b" xml:id="p1.m1">
        <XMath>
          <XMApp>
            <XMTok meaning="equals" role="RELOP">=</XMTok>
            <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">a</XMTok>
            <XMApp>
              <XMTok meaning="minus" role="ADDOP">-</XMTok>
              <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">b</XMTok>
            </XMApp>
          </XMApp>
        </XMath>
      </Math>, and an align-style continuation with an absent left operand <Math mode="inline" tex="=-x" text="absent = - x" xml:id="p1.m2">
        <XMath>
          <XMApp>
            <XMTok meaning="equals" role="RELOP">=</XMTok>
            <XMTok meaning="absent"/>
            <XMApp>
              <XMTok meaning="minus" role="ADDOP">-</XMTok>
              <XMTok font="italic" role="UNKNOWN">x</XMTok>
            </XMApp>
          </XMApp>
        </XMath>
      </Math>.</p>
  </para>
</document>
